From: Jordan Bettcher <thebettcher@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Build against Dart 3.11 / Flutter 3.41: the 3.12 bound is Android-only

Class:   LOCAL WORKAROUND (this distribution ships Flutter 3.41.9 / Dart
         3.11.5; drop this patch when it moves to Flutter >= 3.44).
Applies: open-chess v1.3.0 (patch -p1 from the repository root).
Why:     pubspec.yaml asks for sdk ^3.12.0, and rust_builder/pubspec.yaml for
         sdk >=3.12.0 / flutter >=3.44.0 "for AGP 9's built-in Kotlin
         integration" -- an Android build concern. Every tag back to v1.0.0
         carries the same bounds.
What:    both bounds lowered to 3.11 / 3.41, and pubspec.lock re-resolved by
         `flutter pub get` from the upstream lock on Flutter 3.41.9. Pub kept
         every upstream version except 8, none of which reaches the Linux
         bundle: analyzer and _fe_analyzer_shared, test/test_api/test_core
         (dev tooling), file_selector_android and url_launcher_android
         (Android implementations), and meta 1.18.0 -> 1.17.0 (annotations
         only; 1.17.0 is the version Flutter 3.41 itself pins).
Checked: `flutter analyze lib` at language version 3.11: no issues, so the
         app's Dart uses no 3.12-only language feature.
---
--- a/pubspec.yaml
+++ b/pubspec.yaml
@@ -19,7 +19,7 @@
 version: 1.3.0+5
 
 environment:
-  sdk: ^3.12.0
+  sdk: ^3.11.0
 
 # Dependencies specify other packages that your package needs in order to work.
 # To automatically upgrade your package dependencies to the latest versions
--- a/rust_builder/pubspec.yaml
+++ b/rust_builder/pubspec.yaml
@@ -5,8 +5,8 @@
 
 environment:
   # This local FFI plugin uses AGP 9's built-in Kotlin integration.
-  sdk: '>=3.12.0 <4.0.0'
-  flutter: '>=3.44.0'
+  sdk: '>=3.11.0 <4.0.0'
+  flutter: '>=3.41.0'
 
 dependencies:
   flutter:
--- a/pubspec.lock
+++ b/pubspec.lock
@@ -5,18 +5,18 @@
